CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*priv->dytc)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct ideapad_dytc_priv)...)
#386: FILE: drivers/platform/x86/ideapad-laptop.c:780:
+	priv->dytc = kzalloc(sizeof(struct ideapad_dytc_priv), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

